WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.440
In the last video, we showed you a piece of land,
 right in the middle of our land.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.840
This land is actually not ours...

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.800
Yeah, it's weird, but we will use it anyway, 
because we have trust in the local people!

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.720
So, we cleared up some areas, to see what is there...

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.240
And, we found a lot of old abandoned ruins,
that we could later renovate.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.760
Everything is now cleaned up around the ruin!

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.120
Small room, bigger room!

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.000
But, this will require some paperwork first.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.600
So, to start, we're going to build
a movable house on an old trailer.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.320
And, we're going to get one right now!

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.449
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:50.960
All right, so, we're currently at a place,
where they sell a lot of trailers, vehicles, random stuff...

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.791
We're going to see if we can find a trailer, I guess?

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:57.160
It could also be a truck.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.320
They also have some fridges, but I don't know...

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.320
We're just going to have a look around
to see what they have

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.160
To see what would be a good base,
to recycle for the house.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.640
Let's check it out.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.480
So, here we have one from the circus.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.760
I think they used to sleep in here?

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.735
It's very thin metal and uninsulated

00:01:15.735 --> 00:01:17.840
It could be an option, and it seems like a good size.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:26.840
But, let's see more!

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.720
Another one here!

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.280
And, another circus container!

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.800
Another option is an old big trailer from a truck.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.360
This is way bigger than we need it,
but we could potentially cut it at size.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.120
So, we have the length we want, 
which is also an option and maybe remove a few axils...

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.840
Because, we don't really need them.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.466
Or, we just buy a smaller trailer
like this one here,

00:01:50.466 --> 00:01:56.640
Which is more around the size we're looking for I think,
like, 6 meters, not 12 meters.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.360
So, that's also an option.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.899
I see an another circus one with a cooling box inside?

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.720
Looks a bit raw.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.440
Another option is these cooling boxes,
which they use to transport things.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.720
They're already insulated pretty thick, which is nice.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.800
This one is a bit small,
but you will also have higher ones.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.800
It's also been nastier to work with,
with all the fiberglass and stuff...

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.040
But, it's a decent option since we are
looking for a well insulated thing.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.160
So, it might be nice to recycle one of these things?

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.247
Not sure.

00:02:35.127 --> 00:02:36.736
Maybe, we should renovate this pickup?

00:02:38.065 --> 00:02:38.893
It's a Hilux.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.440
What do you think about renovating this pickup?

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.120
- I see a lot of potential in this vehicle!

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.689
It could be a next project!

00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:55.730
I could also get one of these things.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:01.640
It's the same size as a shipping container, 
which would be, I think, the appropriate size for us.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.000
Which could give a base frame to build upon.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.800
He also has a lot of yarn!

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.112
I don't think we need it at this point, but maybe...

00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:21.707
And also, tires, which he has a lot of too!

00:03:26.685 --> 00:03:29.200
So, we just left this place.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:35.613
You have many interesting vehicles and trailers, 
but apparently, he had another place somewhere close by!

00:03:35.613 --> 00:03:39.720
With some old army vehicles and trailers?

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.756
We're going to check that out!

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.504
- So, this guy what he does apparently 
is to buy broken companies?

00:03:56.343 --> 00:03:58.337
He gets everything and they have!

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:02.280
Machinery, which some parts
 are crap, and some parts are solid...

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.040
Some parts: he modified and fixed!

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.371
He plays around with their waste a bit.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.684
- How is the pickup driving?

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.014
It's amazing!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.920
Are we in trailer land?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.440
- You'll find many funny things!

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.836
We walked around to see what we could find.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.600
So, here we are, at the second place!

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.280
It has much, much more than the previous one!

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:53.960
Let me actually show you some drone shots,
 to really see how many there are!

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.560
So, this place looks pretty impressive from above.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:11.160
It's full of old scrap metal, trailers, and vehicles, 
with a some sort of a big, dug-out mine next to it.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.480
Overall, it looks rough.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.560
Looks like some things have been there
for many years, and rusting away.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.360
Waiting for a new owner!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.800
It's actually nice to see places
like this still exist.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.280
That people see value in reusing these things.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.880
If not, they would melt them into
another metal objects or sent to Africa.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.293
I don't know if you can see it from this camera...

00:05:31.293 --> 00:05:37.200
In here, it's full of trailers, trucks, vehicles, bread boxes...

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.840
Many cool structures, actually!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.120
So, we're going to have a walk around,
to see if something fits.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.720
They have the super nice trailers with a big plateau.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:50.160
So, it's a good base that the other one
didn't have to build up on.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.680
However, you still need to build all of this on top.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.400
So, it would also be cool,
if we can find more of a box...

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:00.560
Because, that means we can just recycle more materials, 
instead of having to build something new here...

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:06.000
Here, you have one with a box on top,
which is kind of a good size for us actually!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.160
I'm not sure what used to be inside.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.840
It ould be anything...

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.840
So, we're going to have a look...

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.208
Looks raw.

00:06:20.818 --> 00:06:22.471
It looks like a toilet.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.932
Showers and a very soft floor...

00:06:33.177 --> 00:06:35.777
It's a very rough box, and a bit dirty...

00:06:35.777 --> 00:06:40.640
Like, it's all this fake wood that got wet,
and expanded, so it's not really solid...

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.960
So, let's continue!

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.240
- This could be maybe our next pickup!

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.066
Look at this interior!

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.816
Nice temperature!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.080
Another cool one!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.842
This one is much higher than usual!

00:07:14.842 --> 00:07:17.383
Four meters or something, I think he said?

00:07:17.383 --> 00:07:19.200
Which is also the problem...

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:22.480
You cannot drive it illegally on the road, or something.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.600
So, it's been here for 20 years.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:28.320
It used to transport bread in France,
which is kind of cool.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:34.120
So, we could potentially make
like a double floor or something in it.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.110
And, it's a lot of space!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.120
It's a bit rough...

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.800
Some old trailers!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.240
They used to move animals in.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.520
Also, it looks like a potential a good house.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.766
But, it might stink too long...

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:53.480
A horse box?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:57.085
Let me show you!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.520
And finally, we have one last one
we saw here from the Army.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:15.280
I think it's like an old trailer,
for the telecommunications or something?

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.683
Sick military stuff!

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.770
Los Angeles, California.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.120
Well, cool stuff inside, but not very useful.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:39.520
But, it's cool!

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.640
- It's a cool place!

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.258
A difficult choice...

00:08:44.418 --> 00:08:45.554
- And, you are hot...

00:08:45.554 --> 00:08:46.450
Oh yeah, I am hot!

00:08:48.345 --> 00:08:49.241
So, that's it!

00:08:49.241 --> 00:08:51.332
We see many trucks, and it's getting very warm now...

00:08:51.332 --> 00:08:52.640
It's time to go.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.120
We're not going to share yet on what we're going to pick!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:03.000
Because, on the one hand, it's cool to take something 
for so many years old, very worn out and really revitalize it again.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.440
But, it's also rough to do it on the land,
because we don't really have a proper closed space...

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.920
So, the moment we start sanding it, or cutting it,
all the paint would blow away into nature.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.003
We don't really have a very industrial area.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:22.440
We want to pick something that is more recyclable,
that is older and rougher, and find a way to properly renovate it.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.280
Or, start a bit cleaner and simpler,
and built more natural on top.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.960
We're not sure yet, and we're going to think about it!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.800
Let us know, if you have any thoughts,
or suggestions on where to go for!

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.440
But, for now, we're going to digest 
and think about all these cool things we've seen!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.440
So, we're now having some lunch,
to think about which trailer we want.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.640
Like, writing down the options.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.440
- We don't know what to do.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:05.265
We tried to make a big list, but we still don't know...

00:10:05.887 --> 00:10:08.819
How are we going to decide this?

00:10:11.207 --> 00:10:12.960
What are you thinking, Dave?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.160
- Maybe someone else would know?

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.000
Who is 'someone else'?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.400
- A whole lot of people, and maybe all together,
they would know the best option...

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.720
Where do we find them?

00:10:25.116 --> 00:10:26.316
- Not in here!

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.796
So, me and Adrian went to visit a scrapyard.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:34.880
We started looking into different kind of trailers,
and boxes that are on top.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:39.200
We couldn't decide, so we figured you guys can decide,
on what house we're going to build.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:44.520
So now, on Patreon, you can vote which option we should go for, 
and we'll pick whatever comes out of the votes!

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.000
Kind of scary to do, but yeah, I hope is going to be okay.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.680
So then, we made a poll on Patreon.

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:54.400
We like to include more people through the decision making process, 
because we feel this project is for everyone!

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.640
So, this seemed like a good try-out!

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.553
We had five different trailers, with each having their pros and cons.

00:10:59.553 --> 00:11:00.840
And, the winner was...

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:02.760
A pig trailer!

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.040
We're currently here to actually buy it.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.400
It's in a very rough condition.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.120
And, as you might have seen, but you chose it anyway!

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.760
Which means: a lot of work for us...

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.440
So, the guys of the scrapyard brought the pig trailer.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.960
They delivered it to the land close by, 
because the yellow truck cannot go on our bumpy roads...

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.240
For that, we need a local tractor.

00:11:33.032 --> 00:11:35.621
We actually also needed to prepare the Middle Land.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:37.920
What do you think about it?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.200
- Rough, but promising!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.715
All right, so, we're currently in the Middle Land.

00:11:51.715 --> 00:11:55.960
We can come here by walking 
a few narrow pathways between the bushes.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.400
But, in order to bring a trailer here,
there's not really a route for that...

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:06.560
And, not that size, at least, because everything around it
is fully overgrown with mimosas and brambles.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:07.960
So, we need to make that!

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.920
But, it turns out it's not that easy...

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.720
So, we need to figure out
where are we going to make it.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.720
Let me show you what our options are.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.448
All right, so, just as a reference,
we're currently here in the Middle Land.

00:12:19.815 --> 00:12:23.852
We have our Basekamp right here,
and a big bottom grass field is here.

00:12:23.852 --> 00:12:28.760
So, on the Middle Land, we had this ruin that we discovered,
and this big middle terrace.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.360
Which is actually lower than all the other parts,
but this is where the trailer needs to go.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.080
Now, there's no route to go there with a big vehicle.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.600
It's fully overgrown with mimosa,
so we need to make it.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:40.750
We have two options:

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:44.880
A route from here, which is the shortest one,
so it seems like it makes sense.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:49.280
Or, a longer one right here,
which is coming from Basekamp.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.640
Now, the shorter one seems nice,
but it actually has a few downsides.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.455
Let me show you.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:57.640
So, the biggest downside is that 
there's a big height difference here...

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:01.040
This is quite a steep wall!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.160
Actually, in the winter, a lot of water flows here.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.360
So, it also erodes the land.

00:13:07.152 --> 00:13:09.520
The road is there, where you can see the little pole.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:15.143
If you want to drive here with a truck,
we need to fully cover this with dirt, so we can drive it.

00:13:15.143 --> 00:13:16.461
Which is a big operation...

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:20.640
And, it probably will flush away in the winter,
 due to the water stream here...

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.920
So, I was just down there.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.080
This is the road where the truck would need to drive.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.080
Which is also a bit of a downside,
that this road is quite narrow for a steep turn there.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:36.120
So, it would be kind of a difficult maneuver,
to turn in a trailer here, to down there...

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.200
Let me show you our second option!

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.880
The second option is right here.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.360
I'm currently near Basekamp, which is behind me.

00:13:43.769 --> 00:13:45.600
The road would need to be here!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:52.920
No real sign of a road yet, but the main upside 
is that there is a road here, here and here.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.840
So, I'm currently at an intersection!

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.960
Which should make it easy for a big truck,
to maneuver and turn around.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:03.120
The big upside is also that there's 
no big height difference here, when you go down.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.240
It's just a slow slope,
and it's a bit of a lengthy one.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.850
We need to make a curve in there,

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:11.354
But then, we would arrive in the second terrace.

00:14:11.354 --> 00:14:17.040
So, this should be a bit more chopping work,
but much more easy to access later on!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:23.720
I think we're going to go for this option,
 and it also has a lot of little mimosas...

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:30.198
And, over here, it's quite dense with a lot of 
very young, thin mimosa sticks.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:33.840
We're going to use this sawblade on the brush cutter.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:40.000
I rarely use this, because it feels a bit rough, 
but it also seems for this purpose it's quite suited!

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.616
It just quickly chops a lot of small, little sticks.

00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:44.960
So, let's see!

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:01.160
So, you might wonder:
''Isn't it bad to chop down all these trees?'' 

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.680
Let me explain your situation with this little oak right here.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:10.400
This oak is a native tree from here, 
and the trees around me are invasive trees called mimosa.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.080
And, they grow fast, like, really fast, 
and much faster than this oak.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:20.240
The downside of that is that they take all the sun, 
from this little oak tree that wants to grow.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:25.560
So, it's a very dominant species,
and it makes it very hard for this little oak to survive.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:30.520
By cleaning up the mimosas,
we get more chances of survival for the native trees.

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:35.600
We hope it helps the ecosystem here also,
 to create a bit more of a resilient forest.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.960
So, we're going to keep all the oaks we see,
like all the native trees, and only clear up the mimosas.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.480
Right now, we are about one-third in.

00:16:10.705 --> 00:16:12.825
I still need to go to there...

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:39.890
Almost there...

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:24.840
Now, we have opened the path 
for the trailer to come, but not really...

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.720
The road itself is still very rough...

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:28.280
Some more work to do.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.000
All right, so, now everything is chopped!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.680
A lot of stuff on the ground.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:34.040
Next up: clean it all up.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.200
But, it's going to be a lot of work...

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.240
So, I'm going to get some help

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.653
After removing all the trees,
we called a local friend with a digger.

00:18:32.653 --> 00:18:35.760
To help us remove the roots,
to make sure they don't stick out.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.040
Hopefully, the mimosas don't grow back fast.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.121
They're currently cleaning up all the mimosa roots,
and really leveling the soil.

00:18:57.121 --> 00:18:59.063
Just so that the pig trailer can come.

00:18:59.063 --> 00:19:01.895
We're currently here in the Middle Land, 
and the trailer is going to be here!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.619
Now, finally, we can move the trailer to land.

00:19:20.948 --> 00:19:24.468
We're not sure if the brakes still work,
and the road is quite narrow and hilly...

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:30.000
So, we put the digger in the back,
to make sure the trailer doesn't drive over the tractor...

00:20:57.722 --> 00:20:58.882
How'd it go?

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:00.720
- Smooth.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.016
Very smooth!

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:05.760
So, here we have the trailer!

00:21:07.298 --> 00:21:08.621
Very beautiful!

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:13.791
There's some new back lights for transport.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.680
It's on the land finally!

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:17.280
Nice!

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:19.190
Let me show you a few things!

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.280
First off, it's blue.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.440
As you might have seen.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:28.360
There's a handle here, of which I have no clue what it does, 
but it turns surprisingly smooth.

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:30.720
So, it feels like it's been used.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.960
A bunch of cables to connect.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:36.040
No idea what they mean...

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:39.760
Looks a bit rusty, but I guess we don't need them!

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:42.920
There's a few small cosmetic holes here and there.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:48.640
Not much profile in the wheels.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.298
Looks like a go-kart or something.

00:21:53.042 --> 00:21:54.522
Yeah, it looks good...

00:21:56.769 --> 00:21:57.960
Here, we have a box.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.560
I have no idea what's inside...

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:01.080
I never opened it.

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:03.400
It's a bit rusty!

00:22:09.708 --> 00:22:10.581
Wow!

00:22:11.654 --> 00:22:13.814
No, it has nothing...

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:16.640
Besides a stone.

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:21.923
So, yeah, here are a bunch of things on the bottom.

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:26.640
I think we could strip it out, 
because I'm not going to use many of that...

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:28.960
I have no idea what any of this is.

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.471
I recognize the wheels.

00:22:39.211 --> 00:22:41.329
So, here we have the beautiful inside.

00:22:45.459 --> 00:22:47.920
Yeah, what can I say?

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.866
It's a little bit rusty on the edges...

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:58.978
Also, the wood is a bit rotten...

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:04.227
And, the roof doesn't really exist...

00:23:06.122 --> 00:23:07.802
I mean: it's something...

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:12.520
You wanted this, Patreon!

00:23:14.274 --> 00:23:16.261
There's some dividers in here.

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:23.480
It's pretty good!

00:23:24.498 --> 00:23:25.818
It needs some paint...

00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:35.406
Some holes in the floor.

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:43.258
This thing looks a bit like a prison!

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:50.160
As you can see, it needs quite some work,
but it's a pretty nice, big size!

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:54.480
So, we're not sure yet what we're going to do, 
because you want to reuse as much as possible.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:59.080
But, overall, the underlying base is pretty solid,
 and the size is also pretty good.

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:01.160
It's like a nice box to build something in.

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:04.080
So, we're also going to start the design, work and planning.

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.480
Like, how do you want to arrange the space?

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:09.840
We are thinking of dividing it,
so we have some sort of a bedroom area.

00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:12.600
Where we can chill, and maybe a wall with a door.

00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:16.868
You have more of a little kitchen,
and a place to relax

00:24:16.868 --> 00:24:18.040
A door there...

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:22.080
Maybe thinking of replacing those,
with a big glass window.

00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:27.480
But, overall, the first rough work that needs to be done
 is to clean it up, and to see the damage.

00:24:27.800 --> 00:24:34.400
Then, insulate the walls, build a frame, build a roof on top, 
and then we can start on the interior.

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:40.120
If you're interested to help out working on a rusty trailer,
you can still sign up below!

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:43.000
You kind of need to be fast,
 because we're going to move fast with this project.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.200
But, yeah, if you want to follow it,
make sure to subscribe!

00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:53.040
Or, continue supporting us on Patreon,
if you want to vote another time.

00:24:53.040 --> 00:24:56.800
Like, when we are going to buy a rusty thing like this...

00:24:57.451 --> 00:24:58.486
Thanks for watching!

00:24:58.486 --> 00:25:00.400
See you in the next video!

